{"diagnosis": "Loopback send of 0xa5 was read back as 0xff, causing TRAP uart data mismatch and tohost FAIL 0xdead. ser_tx is send_pattern[0], so idle must be 1, but reset loads send_pattern <= ~1 whose LSB is 0 and drives a false start on loopback ser_rx. The mis-framed receiver never validates 0xa5, so reg_dat_do stays at idle ~0 (0xff).", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -109,9 +109,9 @@
 	always @(posedge clk) begin
 		if (reg_div_we)
 			send_dummy <= 1;
 		send_divcnt <= send_divcnt + 1;
 		if (!resetn) begin
-			send_pattern <= ~1;
+			send_pattern <= ~0;
 			send_bitcnt <= 0;
 			send_divcnt <= 0;
 			send_dummy <= 1;
", "expected": "tohost PASS, uart loopback 0xa5 matches, checksum changes from 9e1b73c13d0a095f6b9512137fc937a720f9b8a80231ffc4b660d6d1459f6985"}

